// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Objective - Sentinel 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Description :
"P1785929772" "Defeat the Sentinel of Mot"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - Objective 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P3684086542" "You defeated the Sentinel of Mot!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2316570845" "Scirocco has returned as an ally, but Olympian 29 has been absorbed by Mot and Diabolique has gotten away."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P4037463906" "GAH! This is RIDICULOUS!<br><br>{HeroName}, do you know how LONG it took to manufacture an Olympian like number 29?! Who is going to protect me now?! I swear, I was angry before at Diabolique, but now, I am REALLY going to enjoy tearing her apart piece... by... little... <i>piece</i>!<br><br>I received a message, or something, from that Scirocco. He said that him and his skimpy little genie were surveying the graveyard when they saw that ugly little ghost, Diabolique, running away. That's when they held her down.<br><br>That's it, {HeroName}. We are going to end Diabolique, ONCE and for all."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission4 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - Ajax 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page DeanArcDone Text :
"P629564561" "Third time we're meetin', huh {Hero.gender=male cowboy|sweetheart}? I haven't forgotten that whole trick you pulled with that moronic MacArthur punk, but I've been told that I should be letting that lie in the past, so I am.<br><br>Looks like you took care of that ghost chick. Too bad, guess I got here a little too late to lend a hand against her. Anyway, as you probably saw yourself, this Mot creature just broke one of those 'barriers' of power where he can absorb anyone he wants, as evidenced by the Olympian and Diabolique.<br><br>You're <i>probably</i> safe for now; if you hadn't destroyed the Knives of Vengeance, Mot's power would've been way farther than right now. The guy orderin' me around has a proposal for how to help make you immune to Mot's abilities."
// Answer Text :
"P1867300051" "What's this theory?"
// Page Villain Text :
"P2084754460" "Second time we're meetin', huh {Hero.gender=male cowboy|sweetheart}? I normally hate workin' with you villain types, but I've been told I need to put this aside for the greater good, or something..<br><br>Anyway, looks like you took care of that ghost chick. Too bad, guess I got here a little too late to lend a hand against her. Anyway, as you probably saw yourself, this Mot creature just broke one of those 'barriers' of power where he can absorb anyone he wants, as evidenced by the Olympian and Diabolique.<br><br>You're <i>probably</i> safe for now; if you hadn't destroyed the Knives of Vengeance, Mot's power would've been way farther than right now. The guy orderin' me around has a proposal for how to help make you immune to Mot's abilities."
// Page PageBChoice1 Text :
"P415579311" "The key lies in <color yellow>Cimerora</color>. You found out that information about the Circle, yeah?<br><br>The guy givin' me orders said that you're supposed to play a key role in all of that, or that you <i>already</i> did, but now is this time when you go back and actually do it. I don't know, it's time travel stuff, which I frankly can't stand; almost as much as I can't stand the fact that I've been told not to say the name of the guy who's orderin' me around.<br><br>Now, the good thing is that theoretically if you travel back in time to Cimerora right now, you'll come back with barely a few minutes passed, if you're sent back to the right time."
// Answer Text :
"P1278977869" "And how am I supposed to get to Cimerora?"
// Answer Text :
"P1331324725" "Cimerora? From the Midnighter Club?"
// Page PageBChoice1Part2 Text :
"P583165765" "<color orange>Ajax hands you an item with the symbol for the Midnighter club.</color><br><br>I was told to make you an honorary member of the Midnight Squad, a group of secret magic users. The guy up above said that his word can get anyone into the club, even if you are a villain.<br><br>You can get to the Midnighter Mansion in <color yellow>Cap au Diable</color>. From there, you'll wanna use the <color yellow>crystal of fire and ice</color> to get flung back in time to Cimerora.<br><br>Talk to some chick named <color yellow>Sister Solaris</color> when you get there. Things should be set up so that she's been told about Mot, and that you'll arrive in a coincidental time to deal with it.<br><br><color yellow>The guy orderin' me around, said you'd know him as the letter writer, is gonna be there waitin' for you.</color>"
// Answer Text :
"P591590492" "Very well."
// Page PageBChoice2Part2 Text :
"P1673341207" "Yeah, exactly. Shouldn't be a problem, since you're already a member of the group.<br><br>When you get to Cimerora, you'll wanna talk to some chick named <color yellow>Sister Solaris</color> when you get there. Things should be set up so that she's been told about Mot, and that you'll arrive in a coincidental time to deal with it.<br><br><color yellow>The guy orderin' me around, said you'd know him as the letter writer, is gonna be there waitin' for you.</color>"
// Page Regular Text :
"P3524113741" "Second time we're meetin', huh {Hero.gender=male cowboy|sweetheart}? Gotta say, I'm happy to finally work together with a hero this time, I've spent way too much time with villains.<br><br>Anyway, looks like you took care of that ghost chick. Too bad, guess I got here a little too late to lend a hand against her. Anyway, as you probably saw yourself, this Mot creature just broke one of those 'barriers' of power where he can absorb anyone he wants, as evidenced by the Olympian and Diabolique.<br><br>You're <i>probably</i> safe for now; if you hadn't destroyed the Knives of Vengeance, Mot's power would've been way farther than it is at the moment. The guy orderin' me around has a proposal for how to help make you immune to Mot's abilities."
// Page PageCChoice1Part2 Text :
"P3606214980" "<color orange>Ajax hands you an item with the symbol for the Midnighter club.</color><br><br>I was told to make you an honorary member of the Midnight Squad, a group of secret magic users. The guy up above said that his word can get anyone into the club, though I kinda figured someone of your power stature would've been in it already.<br><br>You can get to the Midnighter Mansion in <color yellow>Steel Canyon, Croatoa, or Founders' Falls</color>. From there, you'll wanna use the <color yellow>crystal of fire and ice</color> to get flung back in time to Cimerora.<br><br>Talk to some chick named <color yellow>Sister Solaris</color> when you get there. Things should be set up so that she's been told about Mot, and that you'll arrive in a coincidental time to deal with it.<br><br><color yellow>The guy orderin' me around, said you'd know him as the letter writer, is gonna be there waitin' for you.</color>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - Duncan 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P513003251" "Alright, {HeroName}. I'll get the device going. If Sinclair is right, Diabolique will be trapped.<br><br>By the time you reach her, I should have it ready."
// Answer Text :
"P3936123470" "Alright."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - Detective 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page KnowHopp Text :
"P3662971108" "I remember you, {HeroName}. We met some time ago.<br><br>I have... been in this city for too long. The place was once familiar to me, a home... I called this place home, once. I was... part of the police force here, just a rookie.<br><br>My grandfather was a police officer when the fog first rolled around in the 50's... he always warned me that it would come again, that I would have to be ready to defend our city.<br><br>The fog came, and so did the Pantheon, the zombies. I fought them... but to my shame... my shame...<br><br>I ran, {HeroName}. I heard their voices, calling for my help. But I was out of ammunition, it was suicide. I ran while I heard their voices crying out for me to save them.<br><br>Maybe that's... that's why I ended up back here, from that cursed case."
// Answer Text :
"P3122322440" "Detective Hopps?"
// Page DontKnow Text :
"P2115538362" "I have... been in this city for too long. The place was once familiar to me, a home... I called this place home, once. I was... part of the police force here, just a rookie.<br><br>My grandfather was a police officer when the fog first rolled around in the 50's... he always warned me that it would come again, that I would have to be ready to defend our city.<br><br>The fog came, and so did the Pantheon, the zombies. I fought them... but to my shame... my shame...<br><br>I ran, {HeroName}. I heard their voices, calling for my help. But I was out of ammunition, it was suicide. I ran while I heard their voices crying out for me to save them.<br><br>Maybe that's... that's why I ended up back here, from that cursed case."
// Page HoppsLeaves Text :
"P344204937" "<color orange>Detective Hopp stares at you silently before walking away in a daze.</color>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P1827674586" "Diabolique is stopped now, somewhere within a tunnel system that runs near the graveyard. She's probably gathering her power there.<br><br>I didn't get a chance to use the device Sinclair made before, but now, I <i>will</i>. I'm going to go into that tunnel system with you, {HeroName}, and set the device up at the entrance. It'll prevent Diabolique from doing her little vanishing trick."
// AcceptString :
"P3521162496" "Which will allow us to go after her."
// SendOffString :
"P1135117695" "Precisely. Ooooh, she is going to WISH she didn't cross me. Diabolique does NOT know pain like I do... and I will make sure to savor every delicious minute while I make her endure a ghostly pain like she never could <i>imagine</i>.<br><br>I'm done talking, {HeroName}, it's time for <i>action</i>. <color orange>You had better bring everything you've got, because Diabolique is not going to hold back, not when she's cornered like this.</color>"
// ActiveTaskString :
"P1560297675" "Destroy Diabolique"
// TaskSubTitle :
"P4240069185" "<color deepskyblue>Finale: The Only Way It Could End</color>"

